[{:db/id "q-162346/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6a63e5a4-1602-5e58-b7f4-97d1804e6d78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162346/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "1d01d7e2-2da1-5c2f-9a50-0c74f9e98908" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162346/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "097e2c7f-d1e3-51f5-b6fd-2493c4518988" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162346/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7282e12a-d88e-5401-a1f9-41c022787694" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162346/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d396d329-9e0b-5b3a-9925-b81a2a8c105c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162346/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a7ac790-6055-5386-ad1b-97fce7090478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162346/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-162346/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-162346/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-162346/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-162346/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-162346/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162346" :question/id #uuid "42e88d65-fbab-581f-93da-db30051fb9eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-162346" :question/problem "Let $z$ and $w$ be $4$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${w}^{4}+1=1$\n- ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1$\n- $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ and $w$ are $4$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{4}={w}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n{w}^{4}+1=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4} & =\\frac{{z}^{4}}{{w}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1,$ which means that $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the quotient of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162346/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162346"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162347/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5321a4d9-764a-5f8a-899e-af4eb02fcd4e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162347/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2075c61a-af42-504f-b1d6-6894d3eaa350" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162347/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "631452f4-531e-5022-8057-c343bd82b010" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162347/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "b7d5bb98-d00f-5747-8a9d-0a691ffda7c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162347/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "07099299-dbcf-5ce6-b676-1c1c69d969b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162347/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6ded73b-7a61-5d96-a812-544e399a0958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162347/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-162347/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-162347/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-162347/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-162347/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-162347/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162347" :question/id #uuid "f9d7e6b0-7d90-531b-9d90-fe4de4fcbb33" :question/math-academy-id "q-162347" :question/problem "Let $z$ be a $6$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{2}={z}^{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{6} & =({z}^{6})^{3} \\\\  & =(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement I, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{3})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-162347/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162347"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162368/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "534cf28a-4abf-5838-bd60-312b078838f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162368/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e0aff68f-d033-5475-b4f1-9e1b9172b684" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162368/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "acb82636-e366-59ef-99cb-8dc79db7050a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162368/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "295335a8-40fa-5779-9412-21e787238a43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162368/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b3c66051-46b1-579c-af4f-fc9d1561a2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162368/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a00a1d5a-8491-5e4d-a618-6298b0c3eb69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162368/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-162368/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-162368/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-162368/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-162368/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-162368/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162368" :question/id #uuid "9dad6de4-e17a-5465-968b-8caa846ddbf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162368" :question/problem "Let $z$ be a $4$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${z}^{4}=-1$\n- $(z+z)^{4}=16$\n- $z+z=2z$  is not a $4$th root of unity" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ is a  $4$th root of unity, then (by definition) we have that\n\n$$\n{z}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+z)^{4} & =(2z)^{4} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}\\cdot {z}^{4} \\\\  & =16\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that $(z+z)^{4}\\ne 1,$ which means that $z+z=2z$ is *not* a $4$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162368/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e42234c3-4dbf-5b79-a5ff-11e228be4469"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162368"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281256/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0d7c5f42-6bc1-5cad-8aca-db63f5578062" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281256/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "40e03463-6ce1-5179-8c8e-4b6b3adfcf2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281256/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "51495358-7bce-59cd-99d3-72eff9c94383" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281256/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-281256/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-281256/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281256" :question/id #uuid "5f1224ec-2096-50c1-bcbf-26b6ed16be6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-281256" :question/problem "The sum of all nine $9$th roots of unity is equal to$\\,$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the principal $9$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/9}\\ne 1,\n$$\n\nand that any $9$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,...,8.$  Also, we have ${z}^{9}=1.$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of a geometric sequence, we obtain that the sum of all eight roots is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+z+{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}+{z}^{4}+{z}^{5}+{z}^{6}+{z}^{7}+{z}^{8} & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-{z}^{9})}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-1)}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0}{1-z} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-281256/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ae613d4-e3fe-53cb-b7b0-61596df291d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281256"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319771/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "78be4c2e-1eee-598b-a22c-b75c5d0c61f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319771/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "21438280-2aa9-5a48-bf4f-edf4e775a007" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319771/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-319771/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319771" :question/id #uuid "15d26d14-a520-55b9-aaa0-7122add2005f" :question/math-academy-id "q-319771" :question/problem "The product of all sixteen $16$th roots of unity is equal to$\\,$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the principal $16$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/16}={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/8},\n$$\n\nand that any $16$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,...,15.$ Also, we have ${z}^{16}=1.$\n\nTherefore, the product of all sixteen roots is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{0}\\cdot {z}^{1}\\cdot {z}^{2}\\cdot {z}^{3}\\cdot {z}^{4}\\cdot {z}^{5}\\cdot {z}^{6}\\cdot {z}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{8}\\cdot {z}^{9}\\cdot {z}^{10}\\cdot {z}^{11}\\cdot {z}^{12}\\cdot {z}^{13}\\cdot {z}^{14}\\cdot {z}^{15} & ={z}^{0\\,+\\,1\\,+\\,2\\,+\\,3\\,+\\,4\\,+\\,5\\,+\\,6+\\,⋯+15} \\\\  & ={z}^{120} \\\\  & ={z}^{112+8} \\\\  & ={z}^{112}\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & ={({z}^{16})}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & ={z}^{8} \\\\  & ={({e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/8})}^{8} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-319771/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ae613d4-e3fe-53cb-b7b0-61596df291d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319771"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
